# Ordinary quit/update admission; editor retains all unsaved buffers.
quit-documents-dirty = Save or discard your unsaved documents before continuing.
# Ordinary quit/update admission; original editor write tickets are unsettled.
quit-documents-pending = Wait for document writes to finish, then try again.
# Ordinary quit/update admission; failed writes retain their modified buffers.
quit-documents-failed = A document could not be saved. Resolve it in the editor before continuing.
# Lifecycle progress and additional-window refusal; also used for manual node control.
quit-finalizing = Vessel is finishing the current request.

# Saving app preferences/window state failed; this does not claim a node stop failure.
quit-state-unsaved = Vessel is still open because its settings or window position could not be saved. Try again.
